zed), once per staging session (Establish), and three more times per staged build (VerifyToolchain at build.go:148/219/253 and plan.go:252). Measured atoms: one compiled-scope status = ~3.1s, one real compiled install = ~12.5s, the same scope without a compiled command = 1.08s for a full install plus four status calls.\n\nFAILED ASSUMPTION: the directive assumed repeated expensive setup inside cmd/curator. There is none left. Immutable setup is already shared - the two largest tests build one fixture and one installation and share them across 14 and 6 subtests - and the residual per-subtest cost is three CLI invocations that ARE the assertions (--json row fields, --check exit code, human line). Nothing is memoizable: the toolchain fingerprint is deliberately not, and the operation-private GOCACHE is a hermeticity property. Packaging cannot be split: the tests live in package main, call run() in-process, and assert on unexported identifiers, so a split requires moving run() into an importable package and rewriting ~1500 lines against string literals, which loses compile-time coupling and fails the equivalent-coverage condition. Trimming a task-owned GOROOT mirror is not viable either: src/ is 11006 of 14502 files and stdlib compilation needs it. No masking route (timeout, sharding, -run exclusion, cached results) was used.\n\nOPTION QUANTIFIED: a directory-scoped walk of fingerprintToolchain - descend through per-directory *os.Root handles and reuse the handle of the directory both phases are inside, keeping the identical record set, sort and byte stream - computes the IDENTICAL sha256 and is 2.2x faster (1.64s -> 0.72s per GOROOT, three rounds, identical_digest=true). Prototype in .temp/TASK-260729-2kaopg/probe/main.go; no worktree file was modified. Projected ~35% off cmd/curator (533s -> ~350s) plus material wins in internal/install (289s) and internal/install/atomicity (423s), which pay the same cost. Resolving each component once narrows rather than widens the T